IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cll-careshield`
IMPORT `cll-assessment`

-- CareShield Life and Long-Term Care Act 2019, ss 2(1), 6(2), 7(5)(c), 16, 17, 21(2)(c), 49 and First and Fourth Schedules, with
-- the Disability Assessment Fees Regulations 2020 and reg 26 of the CSHL Scheme Regulations 2020 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case or against MOH's assessment practice (none retrieved). Expected results were written by hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

-- REQ-0278: after a stroke he cannot bathe or dress unaided and can transfer only sometimes. The question says nothing about
-- feeding, toileting or walking; the fixture takes him as managing those without assistance all the time (an assumption).
GIVETH AN ADLs
`Haziq after the stroke` MEANS
    ADLs WITH
        washing      IS `cannot perform it without assistance`
        dressing     IS `cannot perform it without assistance`
        feeding      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        toileting    IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        walking      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        transferring IS `performs it without assistance only sometimes`

GIVETH AN ADLs
`Haziq unable to transfer at all` MEANS
    ADLs WITH
        washing      IS `cannot perform it without assistance`
        dressing     IS `cannot perform it without assistance`
        feeding      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        toileting    IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        walking      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        transferring IS `cannot perform it without assistance`

GIVETH AN ADLs
`fully independent` MEANS
    ADLs WITH
        washing      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        dressing     IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        feeding      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        toileting    IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        walking      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        transferring IS `performs it without assistance all the time`

GIVETH AN ADLs
`needs help bathing only sometimes` MEANS
    ADLs WITH
        washing      IS `performs it without assistance only sometimes`
        dressing     IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        feeding      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        toileting    IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        walking      IS `performs it without assistance all the time`
        transferring IS `performs it without assistance all the time`

GIVETH AN ADLs
`everything only sometimes` MEANS
    ADLs WITH
        washing      IS `performs it without assistance only sometimes`
        dressing     IS `performs it without assistance only sometimes`
        feeding      IS `performs it without assistance only sometimes`
        toileting    IS `performs it without assistance only sometimes`
        walking      IS `performs it without assistance only sometimes`
        transferring IS `performs it without assistance only sometimes`

§ `REQ-0278 (Haziq) -- who assesses, who decides, and how "sometimes" is treated`

-- Who assesses: only an assessor approved by the Minister under s 17(1); the claimant's own doctor is not one unless approved.
#ASSERT `may conduct and report on a disability assessment` `an assessor approved by the Minister under section 17(1)`
#ASSERT NOT `may conduct and report on a disability assessment` `a doctor not approved as an assessor`

-- On a claim, the Administrator may require the assessment and decides the claim.
#ASSERT `who may require the assessment` `a claim under s 16` EQUALS `the Administrator`
#ASSERT `decides whether to accept the claim` `the Administrator`

-- Bathing and dressing are two activities he cannot perform. Transferring "sometimes" is the third only if "sometimes" counts.
#ASSERT `the number of activities the person is unable to perform` `Haziq after the stroke` FALSE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the number of activities the person is unable to perform` `Haziq after the stroke` TRUE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT NOT `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` `Haziq after the stroke` FALSE
#ASSERT `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` `Haziq after the stroke` TRUE
#ASSERT `the result turns on how sometimes is read` `Haziq after the stroke`

-- Under the Fourth Schedule "sometimes" is not "all the time": he is not "not disabled" either way.
#ASSERT `the number of activities needing assistance at some time` `Haziq after the stroke` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT NOT `is not disabled on the assessed activities` `Haziq after the stroke`

-- A stroke is not an excluded cause under reg 26.
#ASSERT NOT `the cause is a prescribed excluded event` `a stroke or other illness`

-- The assessor's fee: $100 at his place of practice, $250 at home or in hospital (inclusive of GST).
#ASSERT `the assessment fee is within the cap` 100 `the assessor's place of practice`
#ASSERT `the assessment fee is within the cap` 250 `any other premises`

§ `First and Fourth Schedules -- other patterns`

#ASSERT `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` `Haziq unable to transfer at all` FALSE
#ASSERT `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` `Haziq unable to transfer at all` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the result turns on how sometimes is read` `Haziq unable to transfer at all`

#ASSERT `is not disabled on the assessed activities` `fully independent`
#ASSERT `the number of activities the person is unable to perform` `fully independent` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` `fully independent` TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `is not disabled on the assessed activities` `needs help bathing only sometimes`
#ASSERT NOT `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` `needs help bathing only sometimes` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the result turns on how sometimes is read` `needs help bathing only sometimes`

#ASSERT `the number of activities the person is unable to perform` `everything only sometimes` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the number of activities the person is unable to perform` `everything only sometimes` TRUE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the result turns on how sometimes is read` `everything only sometimes`

-- Entitlement under s 12(2) (existing module) on Haziq's count under each reading, claim accepted, cover not ended.
#ASSERT `is entitled to the insured sum` TRUE (`the number of activities the person is unable to perform` `Haziq after the stroke` TRUE) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to the insured sum` TRUE (`the number of activities the person is unable to perform` `Haziq after the stroke` FALSE) TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 6(2), 7(5)(c), 16(3)(c), 21(2)(c) -- when an assessment may be required, and by whom`

#ASSERT `an assessment may be required` `a periodic disability review under s 21`
#ASSERT `an assessment may be required` `an application for cover under s 7`
#ASSERT NOT `an assessment may be required` `a premium deduction from MediSave`
#ASSERT `who may require the assessment` `an application for cover under s 7` EQUALS `the Board`
#ASSERT `who may require the assessment` `ascertaining disability for automatic cover under s 6(1)(b) or (c)` EQUALS `the Board`
#ASSERT `who may require the assessment` `a periodic disability review under s 21` EQUALS `the Administrator`

#ASSERT `pays the insured sum` `the Board`
#ASSERT NOT `pays the insured sum` `the Administrator`
#ASSERT NOT `decides whether to accept the claim` `a family member`

§ `s 17(2) and S 69/2020 -- fee caps`

#ASSERT `the maximum assessment fee including GST` `the assessor's place of practice` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the maximum assessment fee including GST` `any other premises` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT NOT `the assessment fee is within the cap` 150 `the assessor's place of practice`
#ASSERT NOT `the assessment fee is within the cap` 251 `any other premises`

§ `s 49 -- fraudulent assessment`

#ASSERT `the assessor commits an offence under section 49` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the assessor commits an offence under section 49` TRUE FALSE

-- Overpayment $5,000 plus fee $250 = $5,250; times 4 = $21,000. No overpayment, fee $100: 4 x 100 = $400.
#ASSERT `the section 49 penalty` 5000 250 EQUALS 21000
#ASSERT `the section 49 penalty` 0 100 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the section 49 maximum fine` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the section 49 maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 24

-- If prescribed as compoundable (not retrieved): lower of half of $10,000 and $1,000 = $1,000 (s 56(1), existing module).
#ASSERT `the most a composition can be` `the section 49 maximum fine` EQUALS 1000

§ `s 16(4)(d) and reg 26 -- excluded causes`

#ASSERT `the cause is a prescribed excluded event` `war`
#ASSERT `the cause is a prescribed excluded event` `a terrorist act`
#ASSERT `the cause is a prescribed excluded event` `hostility, whether war is declared or not`
#ASSERT NOT `the cause is a prescribed excluded event` `an accident`
